V-race #2 RESIDUAL guard (firmware-only, NO rebuild): validate the k_thread pointer
in the eager V save/restore; skip + record if WILD. Prevents the residual atomic
mcause-5 wild vse8.v STORE at its source (wild save_to) and the wild vle8.v LOAD
(observed at z_riscv_vstate_restore_thread+0x7e, a0 = clobbered switch_handle).
Applies ON TOP of the is_dirty init-guard + the vstart/fence v.c patch. Orthogonal
to 6f53ddc6c/backend-gate (RTL). Diagnostic globals z_riscv_v_dbg_wild_{save,restore}
[_ptr] capture the wild pointer + which path -- KEY to locating the upstream source:
if wild_save fires -> the wild store source is a save with a clobbered thread ptr;
if only wild_restore fires -> the switch_handle was clobbered by something else.
Valid k_thread range = [CONFIG_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS, +CONFIG_SRAM_SIZE KiB) =
[0x80000000, 0xC0000000) for the drone. APPLY: git apply; rebuild firmware; multi-run
ATOMIC build_rocc_gated xN -> N/N clean = wild store/load prevented (and read the
dbg_wild_* globals to see the culprit). Interim/diagnostic: a wild a0 still means a
lost thread, so also validate a0 in z_riscv_switch if a hard fix is needed.

